    <h1>Accessibility Statement</h1>
    <p>Last updated: June 8, 2026</p>
    <p>I want HighSpeedRail.TV to work for everyone, including people who use screen readers, keyboard navigation, or other assistive technology.</p>
    <h2>What I aim for</h2>
    <p>I build toward the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at the AA level: readable contrast, pages you can navigate by keyboard, real descriptions on images, and headings that follow a sensible order.</p>
    <h2>Where it stands</h2>
    <p>This is a small project I maintain on my own, so treat it as a work in progress rather than a certified result. The embedded YouTube player also brings its own controls that I don't have much say over.</p>
    <h2>Found a barrier?</h2>
    <p>If something here is hard to use with assistive technology, I'd genuinely like to hear about it. Tell me which page and what got in your way, and I'll fix what I can. Email hello@highspeedrail.tv.</p>
  </div>
</section>
